ia.</article-title><person-group person-group-type="editor"><name><surname>Johnson</surname><given-names>LR</given-names></name></person-group><source>Physiology of the Gastrointestinal tract</source><publisher-loc>New-York</publisher-loc><publisher-name>Raven Press</publisher-name><fpage>795</fpage><lpage>877</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0000612-Hannun1"><label>6</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hannun</surname><given-names>YA</given-names></name></person-group><year>1994</year><article-title>The sphingomyelin cycle and the second messenger function of ceramide.</article-title><source>J Biol Chem</source><volume>269</volume><fpage>3125</fpage><lpage>3128</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8106344</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0000612-Hannun2"><label>7</label><citation citation-type="book"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hannun</surname><given-names>YA</given-names></name></person-group><year>1997</year><article-title>Sphingolipid-mediated signal transduction.</article-title><publisher-loc>Heidelberg</publisher-loc><publisher-name>Springer</publisher-name><fpage>188</fpage></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0000612-Liu1"><label>8</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Liu</surname><given-names>G</given-names></name><name><surname>Kleine</surname><given-names>L</given-names></name><name><surname>Hebert</surname><given-names>RL</given-names></name></person-group><year>1999</year><article-title>Advances in the signal transduction of ceramide and related sphingolipids.</article-title><source>Crit Rev Cl Lab Sci</source><volume>36</volume><fpage>511</fpage><lpage>573</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0000612-Obeid1"><label>9</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Obeid</surname><given-names>LM</given-names></name><name><surname>Linardic</surname><given-names>CM</given-names></name><name><surname>Karolak</surname><given-names>LA</given-names></name><name><surname>Hannun</surname><given-names>YA</given-names></name></person-group><year>1993</year><article-title>Programmed cell death induced by ceramide.</article-title><source>Science</source><volume>259</volume><fpage>1769</fpage><lpage>1771</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8456305</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0000612-Bielawska1"><label>10</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Bielawska</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name><name><surname>Crane</surname><given-names>HM</given-names></name><name><surname>Liotta</surname><given-names>D</given-names></name><name><surname>Obeid</surname><given-names>LM</given-names></name><name><surname>Hannun</surname><given-names>YA</given-names></name></person-group><year>1993</year><article-title>Selectivity of ceramide-mediated biology. Lack of activity of erythro-dihydroceramide.</article-title><source>J Biol Chem</source><volume>268</volume><fpage>26226</fpage><lpage>26232</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">8253743</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0000612-Luberto1"><label>11</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Luberto</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Hassler</surname><given-names>DF</given-names></name><name><surname>Signorelli</surname><given-names>P</given-names></name><name><surname>Okamoto</surname><given-names>Y</given-names></name><name><surname>Sawai</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2002</year><article-title>Inhibition of tumor necrosis factor-induced cell death in MCF7 by a novel inhibitor of neutral sphingomyelinase.</article-title><source>J Biol Chem</source><volume>277</volume><fpage>41128</fpage><lpage>41139</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12154098</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0000612-Marchesini1"><label>12</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Marchesini</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Luberto</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Hannun</surname><given-names>YA</given-names></name></person-group><year>2003</year><article-title>Biochemical properties of mammalian neutral sphingomyelinase 2 and its role in sphingolipid metabolism.</article-title><source>J Biol Chem</source><volume>278</volume><fpage>13775</fpage><lpage>13783</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">12566438</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0000612-Zundel1"><label>13</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Zundel</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name><name><surname>Swiersz</surname><given-names>LM</given-names></name><name><surname>Giaccia</surname><given-names>A</given-names></name></person-group><year>2000</year><article-title>Caveolin 1-mediated regulation of receptor tyrosine kinase-associated phosphatidylinositol 3-kinase activity by ceramide.</article-title><source>Mol Cell Biol</source><volume>20</volume><fpage>1507</fpage><lpage>1514</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10669728</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0000612-Chavesde1"><label>14</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Chaves (de)</surname><given-names>EP</given-names></name><name><surname>Bussiere</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>MacInnis</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Vance</surname><given-names>DE</given-names></name><name><surname>Campenot</surname><given-names>RB</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2001</year><article-title>Ceramide inhibits axonal growth and nerve growth factor uptake without compromising the viability of sympathetic neurons.</article-title><source>J Biol Chem</source><volume>276</volume><fpage>36207</fpage><lpage>36214</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11454862</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0000612-Vieu1"><label>15</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Vieu</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Terce</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Chevy</surname><given-names>F</given-names></name><name><surname>Rolland</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Barbaras</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2002</year><article-title>Coupled assay of sphingomyelin and ceramide molecular species by gas liquid chromatography.</article-title><source>J Lipid Res</source><volume>43</volume><fpage>510</fpage><lpage>522</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11893787</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0000612-Ogretmen1"><label>16</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Ogretmen</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Pettus</surname><given-names>BJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Rossi</surname><given-names>MJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Wood</surname><given-names>R</given-names></name><name><surname>Usta</surname><given-names>J</given-names></name><etal/></person-group><year>2002</year><article-title>Biochemical mechanisms of the generation of endogenous long chain ceramide in response to exogenous short chain ceramide in A489 human lung adenocarcinoma cell line. Role for endogenous ceramide in mediating the action of exogenous ceramide.</article-title><source>J Biol Chem</source><volume>277</volume><fpage>12960</fpage><lpage>12969</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11815611</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="pone.0000612-Jaffrezou1"><label>17</label><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Jaffrezou</surname><given-names>JP</given-names></name><name><surname>Maestre</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name